STACKS AND QUEUES

Stack:
	A specialized data storage structure
		- Access is restricted however
	The stack has two main functions, push and pop
		- Insertion is done with push, and removal is done with pop
	Stack allows access to only the last element entered into the stack
		- Last-in-First-out (LIFO) list

Stack functions:
	Push
		- inserts an item into the top of the stack
		- top points to the newly added item
		- check if stack is full?
	Pop
		- removes an item from the top of the stack
		- top points to one before the removed item
		- check empty condition?

Stack implementation:
	2 basic implementations:
	Array-based implementation
		- Simple and efficient, but the maximum size of the stack is fixed
	Singly Linked List-based implementation
		- Complicated, but there is no limit on stack size (size is subject to available memory)

